-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner automorphism wₚ over ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ and $p$ be non-zero natural numbers with $p$ prime and $p \nmid N_0$. Write $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and let $\overline{F}_{N} =$ [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldBar N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L111) be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `divisorExpansions N`. The assertion is the existence of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $w$ of $\overline{F}_{N_0 p}$ with the following property for every non-zero $d$ dividing $N_0$ and every element $x$ of $\overline{F}_{N_0 p}$: first, if the Laurent series underlying $x$ is the image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ d jq` — that is, the $q$-expansion $j(q^{d})$, where `jq` is $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ` and `qExpand` is the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$ on exponents — then the series underlying $w(x)$ is `qExpand` at $p$ applied to that same series, i.e. $j(q^{dp})$; and second, conversely, if the series underlying $x$ is $j(q^{dp})$ in this spelling, then the series underlying $w(x)$ is $j(q^{d})$. The conclusion is phrased as these two implications about an arbitrary $x$, so it does not by itself assert that the two series in question lie in $\overline{F}_{N_0 p}$.
--
--   This is the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ of $X_0(N_0 p)$ for $p \nmid N_0$, realised as an automorphism of the function field after base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and pinned down by its effect $j(q^{d}) \leftrightarrow j(q^{dp})$ on the $q$-expansions attached to divisors $d$ of $N_0$. It feeds the comparison of the two degeneracy maps $X_0(N_0p) \to X_0(N_0)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and thence the Hecke-operator identities used there, being cited by [`ModularCurve.coeff_diffQExpBar_heckeDiffBar_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coeff_diffQExpBar_heckeDiffBar_of_not_dvd), [`ModularCurve.exists_regularProlongation_modularFunctionFieldBar_mul_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_regularProlongation_modularFunctionFieldBar_mul_of_not_dvd) and related results.
